# ARP > TRSP: a key is a transposition from middle C that the track keeps until the next key
tapkey b5
expect trk 5
tap ARP
expect view 4
turn K1 5
expect arpmode 5
expect trans 0
shot trsp_0.png
tap PLAY
wait 300
# key 14 = F3 + 14 = note 67: seven semitones above middle C (60); the keys do not play notes themselves, the sequence moves
key 14 down
wait 100
expect trans 7
expect arpn 0
key 14 up
wait 100
expect trans 7
shot trsp_7.png
# a key below middle C goes down; middle C itself (key 7) is no transposition
key 3 down
wait 100
key 3 up
expect trans -4
key 7 down
wait 100
key 7 up
expect trans 0
# the octave buttons move the whole keyboard: the same key is an octave up
tap OCT+
key 7 down
wait 100
key 7 up
expect trans 12
tap SEQ
shot trsp_seq.png
# leaving the mode puts the track back
tap ARP
turn K1 -1
expect arpmode 4
expect trans 0
tap PLAY
